adr: 0301
file: lsp/pasls.pas
kills: lsp-server
why: A name is in scope only where the block that declares it contains the position, and the rows of --dump-symbols nest by depth with a block's extent on the declaration that opens it (ADR-0253). Calling every row visible offers `Inner`'s parameters and its local in the program's own statement part, which is the second half of lsp/sessions/completion.out.
--- old
            inside := depth = 0;
            found := depth = 0;
--- new
            inside := true;
            found := true;
